// @status: GENERAL
// @invariant: resume_capture_schema_unnameable
// @dimension: direct invalid — a capture whose type this build cannot name
//
// The capture is an anonymous record. It has a structure and no nominal
// identity, so nothing says what schema the manifest should record. The hash
// would be derived from a guess, and a guessed hash matches nothing — every
// resume of this handler would fail after deployment, for a reason unreadable
// from the deployment.
//
// **This witness was invalid evidence until 2026-08-10.** It was written as
// `let derived = helper(store_id)` with `helper` declared nowhere, and it was
// caught — but for the wrong reason. `helper` resolved to nothing, so `derived`
// had no type, so the schema was unnameable. The subject is a type that CANNOT
// be named; what was being exercised was a call that did not exist. Declaring
// `helper` with a return type made the witness go silent, which is what
// surfaced it. An anonymous record is the shape the invariant is actually
// about, and it depends on no resolution failure.

module generality.schema_unnameable

import domain.{ StoreId }

fn refresh(id: StoreId) -> () !{} { todo }

view Panel(store_id: StoreId) !{} {
    let derived = { id: store_id }
    <button on:press={resumable(captures = { derived }) => refresh(derived)}>
        Refresh
    </button>
}
